        "comments": "The assembly lpSpaEmer1.hap1.2 is based on 52x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome contains a number of heterozygous inversions on the following chromosomes: chromosome 5 (23.4-24.2Mbp) and chromosome 6 (16.9-18.8Mbp). There is also a heterozygous translocation on chromosome 10 (13.5-13.8 Mbp).",
